15 0 obj
<< /A 38 0 R /Alt (Panel a shows a flowchart from the TriNetX US Collaborative Network identifying atopic dermatitis \(AD\) eligible and non-AD eligible patients using ICD-10 codes, followed by propensity score matching, resulting in matched AD and non-AD cohorts of 351,069 patients each. Panel b displays a flowchart from the same network identifying biologic-eligible and conventional systemic immunosuppressant \(cvIS\) eligible patients, with matching on fourteen covariates, resulting in biologic and cvIS cohorts of 5,439 patients each.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 27 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 39 0 R /Alt (Panel a shows a radar chart comparing psoriasis vulgaris and topical betamethasone risk with three negative controls: appendectomy, presbycusis, and burns. Panel b is a line graph showing higher cumulative incidence of topical betamethasone use for atopic dermatitis cases versus controls over time, with hazard ratio 2.41 and significant p-value. Panel c displays similar cumulative incidence curves for appendectomy between atopic dermatitis cases and controls, with a hazard ratio near one and non-significant p-value. Panel d depicts a much higher cumulative incidence of psoriasis in cases compared to controls, with hazard ratio 3.81 and significant p-value.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 30 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 40 0 R /Alt (Two-panel figure displays cumulative incidence curves with shaded confidence intervals over six hundred days for cases treated with biologics and controls. Panel a shows a significantly lower psoriasis risk in biologics \(blue\) versus controls \(orange\) with hazard ratio zero point two and significant log-rank p-value. Panel b displays similar cumulative incidence between biologics and controls for the aggregate negative control outcome, with a non-significant hazard ratio of one point two and log-rank p-value.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 41 0 R /Alt (Line graph comparing EHRs with documented exposure to Dupilumab \(circles\) and cvIS \(triangles\) from 2015 to 2023. Dupilumab exposures rise sharply after its 2017 approval, while cvIS remains steady.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
